Group E of the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]] consisted of [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]], [[Ecuador national football team|Ecuador]], [[France national football team|France]], and [[Honduras national football team|Honduras]]. Play began on 15 June and ended on 25 June 2014. The top two teams, France and Switzerland, advanced to the round of 16.

