==Matches==
===Switzerland vs Ecuador===
The two teams had never met before.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=16 |title=2014 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit |publisher=FIFA.com |page=16 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140629232249/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf |archivedate=29 June 2014 }}</ref>

Ecuador took the lead in the first half when [[Walter Ayoví]]'s free kick was headed in by [[Enner Valencia]]. Switzerland equalised early in the second half from another set-piece, [[Ricardo Rodríguez (footballer)|Ricardo Rodríguez]]'s corner kick headed in by half-time substitute [[Admir Mehmedi]].<ref>{{cite web|url = https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/15/switzerland-ecuador-world-cup-2014-group-e-match-report|title= Switzerland sink Ecuador in nick of time as Haris Seferovic secures justice|date= 15 June 2014 |work=Guardian|accessdate=30 October 2014}}</ref>
The winning goal of the match was scored by another substitute [[Haris Seferovic]] in the 93rd minute of the game with just 20 seconds remaining in injury time. A Swiss breakaway started in their own penalty area when [[Valon Behrami]] won the ball, and finished by Seferovic converting Rodríguez's cross.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/06/15/sports/worldcup/world-cup-switzerland-vs-ecuador.html?_r=0 |title=World Cup 2014: Switzerland Stuns Ecuador, 2-1, in Added Time|newspaper=The New York Times|date=15 June 2014|accessdate=15 June 2014}}</ref>

This was Switzerland's first World Cup win over South American opposition in six attempts.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25285085|title=Switzerland 2 Ecuador 1|work=BBC Sport|date=15 June 2014}}</ref>

