===France vs Honduras===
The two teams had never met before.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=17 |title=2014 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit |publisher=FIFA.com |page=17 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140629232249/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf |archivedate=29 June 2014 }}</ref>

The match started without the national anthems being played before the kick-off,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.foxnews.com/sports/france-and-honduras-kick-off-without-singing-national-anthems-at-world-cup/|title=France and Honduras kick off without singing national anthems at World Cup|publisher=Fox News|date=15 June 2014|access-date=15 June 2014}}</ref> which FIFA later said was due to an audio system malfunction.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.smh.com.au/fifa-world-cup-2014/world-cup-match-report/world-cup-2014-france-thrash-honduras-as-history-made-20140616-zs8t0.html|title=World Cup 2014: France thrash Honduras as history made|newspaper=The Sydney Morning Herald|date=16 June 2014}}</ref> France took the lead in the first half on a penalty kick converted by [[Karim Benzema]], which was awarded on a foul by [[Wilson Palacios]] on [[Paul Pogba]], for which Palacios received his second yellow card and was sent off.<ref>{{cite web|url = https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/15/france-honduras-world-cup-2014-group-e-match-report|title=France's Karim Benzema makes 10-man Honduras pay for tough line|date= 15 June 2014 |work=Guardian|accessdate=30 October 2014}}</ref>
An own goal by Honduras goalkeeper [[Noel Valladares]] early in the second half gave France a two-goal lead. Benzema's shot rebounded off the post and then hit Valladares, and despite his effort to scoop it clear, the ball was indicated by [[goal-line technology]] to have crossed the line and the goal was awarded. The goal was the first time that a goal was awarded in the World Cup with the support of [[goal-line technology]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.nydailynews.com/sports/soccer/benzema-france-10-man-honduras-article-1.1830806|title=2014 World Cup: Karim Benzema, France too much for 10-man Honduras|newspaper=New York Daily News|date=15 June 2014|accessdate=15 June 2014}}</ref> There was some confusion when the animated replay of the goal was shown in the stadium, however, as when the ball first hit the post, causing "NO GOAL" to correctly flash onto screens in the stadium, it then hit Valladares and crossed the line, producing "GOAL" on the screen. The initial flash of "NO GOAL" drew boos from fans, caused a commotion among the managers and players on the sideline,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.goal.com/en-sg/news/3999/world-cup-2014/2014/06/16/4886951/suarez-baffled-by-goal-line-technology|title=Suarez baffled by goal-line technology|publisher=Goal.com|date=16 June 2014}}</ref> and led to confusion even from the [[BBC]]'s experienced television commentator [[Jonathan Pearce (commentator)|Jonathan Pearce]], who required his colleague [[Martin Keown]] to explain the incident to him.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/sport/row-zed/bbcs-jonathan-pearce-utterly-baffled-3701145|title=BBC's Jonathan Pearce utterly baffled by goal-line technology|work=Daily Mirror|date=15 June 2014|accessdate=15 June 2014}}</ref> In response to the confusion, FIFA promised to review how the replays are shown in the future for similar incidents.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=france-score-first-world-cup-goal-to-be-awarded-with-the-support-of-gl-2373179.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140617084804/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=france-score-first-world-cup-goal-to-be-awarded-with-the-support-of-gl-2373179.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=17 June 2014|title=France score first World Cup goal to be awarded with the support of GLT|publisher=FIFA.com|date=16 June 2014}}</ref> 
France completed the scoring when Benzema scored his second goal, as he blasted in the rebound after [[Mathieu Debuchy]]'s shot was inadvertently blocked by [[Patrice Evra]] and fell to him in the penalty area.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25285092|title=France 3 Honduras 0|work=BBC Sport|date=15 June 2014}}</ref>

Stretching back to their last match of the 1982 World Cup, this was the fifth consecutive World Cup match that Honduras failed to score a goal, matching the record held by Bolivia (1930–1994) and Algeria (1986–2010).<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://sunnewsonline.com/new/?p=68200|location=Lagos, Nigeria|title=World Cup Fact Files|date=17 June 2014|newspaper=[[The Sun (Nigeria)|The Sun]]}}</ref>

