===Honduras vs Ecuador===
The two teams had met in 14 previous matches, all in friendlies, most recently in 2013, a 2–2 draw.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=33 |title=2014 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit |publisher=FIFA.com |page=33 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140629232249/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf |archivedate=29 June 2014 }}</ref> The two coaches, fellow Colombians [[Luis Fernando Suárez]] and [[Reinaldo Rueda]], had previously managed their opponents: Suárez managed Ecuador in the 2006 World Cup, while Rueda managed Honduras in the 2010 World Cup.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=mixed-emotions-for-suarez-and-rueda-2376456.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140619123547/http://www.fifa.com//worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=mixed-emotions-for-suarez-and-rueda-2376456.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=19 June 2014|title=Mixed emotions for Suarez and Rueda|publisher=FIFA.com|date=19 June 2014}}</ref> Honduras midfielder [[Wilson Palacios]] was suspended for the match, having received a red card against France.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.supersport.com/football/world-cup-2014/news/140617/Palacios_Pereira_hit_with_onegame_bans |title=Palacios, Pereira hit with one-game bans |publisher=[[SuperSport (South African broadcaster)|SuperSport]] |date=17 June 2014 |accessdate=17 June 2014}}</ref>

Honduras took the lead in the first half when [[Carlo Costly]] collected left back [[Brayan Beckeles]]'s long clearance to score with his left foot.<ref>{{cite web|url = https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/21/world-cup-2014-honduras-ecuador-match-report|title=Enner Valencia's double takes Ecuador beyond Honduras|date= 21 June 2014 |work=Guardian|accessdate=30 October 2014}}</ref>
Ecuador, which needed at least a point to stay alive in the competition, equalised three minutes later when [[Juan Carlos Paredes|Juan Paredes]]'s shot was deflected and [[Enner Valencia]] turned the ball in at the far post from close range. Enner Valencia scored the game winner in the second half, heading in a free kick from [[Walter Ayoví]].<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25285214|title=Honduras 1 Ecuador 2|work=BBC Sport|date=20 June 2014}}</ref>

Costly's goal snapped Honduras's 511-minute World Cup scoreless streak stretching back to 1982, second place at the time to the record of 517 minutes between 1930 and 1990 held by Bolivia.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/2014/06/20/costly-helps-lift-the-burden-from-honduras-laing/11201157/|title=Costly helps lift the burden from Honduras' Laing|newspaper=USA Today|date=20 June 2014}}</ref> Enner Valencia's brace gave him three total goals in the tournament, and he joined [[Agustín Delgado]] as the country's joint top scorer in the World Cup.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=valencia-i-sold-milk-to-buy-football-boots-2379692.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140621185347/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=valencia-i-sold-milk-to-buy-football-boots-2379692.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=21 June 2014|title=Valencia: I sold milk to buy football boots|publisher=FIFA.com|date=21 June 2014}}</ref>

