===Ecuador vs France===
The two teams had met in one previous match, in a friendly in 2008, won 2–0 by France.<ref name=StatKit45 /> France midfielder [[Yohan Cabaye]] was suspended for the match due to accumulation of yellow cards.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.goal.com/fr/news/4959/international/2014/06/20/4900162/mondial-2014-bleus-cabaye-suspendu-face-%C3%A0-lequateur|title=Mondial 2014, Bleus : Cabaye suspendu face à l'Equateur|language=French|publisher=Goal.com|date=20 June 2014}}</ref>

The match finished goalless, with the point enough to confirm France's place in the knockout stage, winning the group with seven points. Ecuador, which had to match Switzerland's result in the final match to have any chance of qualification, had captain [[Antonio Valencia]] sent off in the second half after a high tackle on [[Lucas Digne]].<ref>{{cite web|url = https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/25/ecuador-france-world-cup-2014-group-e-match-report|title= France top group after failing to break down battling 10-man Ecuador|date= 25 June 2014 |work=Guardian|accessdate=30 October 2014}}</ref>
As Switzerland defeated Honduras in the other match played at the same time, Ecuador was eliminated, thus being the only team in the CONMEBOL group to fail to advance to the Round of 16.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25285420|title=Ecuador 0 France 0|work=BBC Sport|date=25 June 2014}}</ref>

